1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,040
This is it.

3
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,167
What?

4
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:43,918
Goodbye, Go Eun-sae.

5
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:47,964
What do you mean?
Where are you telling me to go, alone?

6
00:00:50,925 --> 00:00:56,305
Jang Tae-ha!

7
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:57,473
<i>Jang Tae-ha.</i>

8
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:58,808
Jang Tae-ha!

9
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:11,780
What's with the strange dream?

10
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,157
Actually, no.

11
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:16,409
<i>What about our marriage?</i>

12
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,286
Is that not happening?

13
00:01:22,832 --> 00:01:24,250
I guess it isn't that strange,

14
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:26,586
since he doesn't even like me.

15
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:39,098
<i>Now that her memory has returned,
this whole act is over.</i>

16
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:42,101
<i>Pretending to be her boyfriend,
being all close…</i>

17
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:44,104
<i>Starting tomorrow, you can't do that.</i>

18
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:14,259
Are you okay?

19
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:17,344
Don't act as if you care.

20
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:19,305
I know now that you don't.

21
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:23,017
So you remember all of it?

22
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:29,106
What kind of person Jang Tae-ha really is.

23
00:02:29,107 --> 00:02:31,025
I know everything now.

24
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:34,320
Yes.

25
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,906
So what will you do now?

26
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:41,119
Now that everything's out in the open,
are you going to be honest?

27
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:43,412
I know you must be confused.

28
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:45,748
I'm sorry if our time together
was unpleasant.

29
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:50,586
It was the best I could do.
Pretending we dated to bring you here.

30
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:52,130
I couldn't leave you alone.

31
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:54,924
Why not?

32
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:56,551
Because you pitied me?

33
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:02,432
I may have lost my memory,
but I never asked for sympathy.

34
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,812
Why didn't you just abandon me?

35
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,691
As you now know,

36
00:03:12,483 --> 00:03:13,526
you have to leave.

37
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:17,989
I found a place for you to go.

38
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:22,660
You can leave next week. Until then,
stay here even if it's uncomfortable.

39
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:27,373
Sorry for everything.

40
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:38,050
So people really do change overnight.

41
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:39,886
I've just gone back to my old self.

42
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:53,233
I really can't believe any of this,
so I'll ask you one last time.

43
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:57,862
So you're saying
that everything you said and did for me

44
00:03:58,363 --> 00:03:59,572
was all fake?

45
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:02,784
Yes.

46
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,286
That it was all an act?

47
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:07,914
Yes.

48
00:04:13,586 --> 00:04:14,420
Go Eun-sae.

49
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,551
Why did you have to…

50
00:04:21,052 --> 00:04:22,387
Get a grip, Go Eun-sae!

51
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:29,435
This isn't the time to get angry.

52
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:31,771
It's time for you to leave.

53
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:41,781
Stay here. I'll go buy some ointment.

54
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:05,263
JUNGANG PHARMACY

55
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:18,401
Go Eun-sae.

56
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,045
Go Eun-sae!

57
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:41,257
Go Eun-sae!

58
00:05:49,932 --> 00:05:52,267
If she remembered it all,
she should've been terrified.

59
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,810
Where on earth did she go?

60
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:56,856
You don't think she went
to the Seoul Prosecutor's Office, do you?

61
00:05:58,274 --> 00:06:01,319
Seoul is Baek Sang-gil's turf,
so she could be in real danger.

62
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:03,154
And she left her phone.

63
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:07,199
The fastest way to find her would be
to check the cameras from here to town.

64
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,868
We'd need to report her missing,
but her identity is…

65
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:12,287
Hey, don't worry about that.

66
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:16,667
I've been drinking buddies with
the local police chief for a decade.

67
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,051
Is there a party going on?

68
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,886
Why are you all swarming out?

69
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,514
Where's our girl, Eun-sae?

70
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,474
Did you happen to see her?

71
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:34,434
What are you talking about?

72
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:37,230
- We made it over here to comfort her.
- Comfort her?

73
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:41,316
There's no such thing as secrets
in a teeny village like this.

74
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:44,694
I heard she drank heaps
at the pub yesterday

75
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:48,574
because someone left her
completely torn up inside.

76
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:50,493
Sorry?

77
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:55,122
Fine! I'll say a few words as your elder.

78
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,456
You, Tae-ha!

79
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:57,833
You shouldn't do that.

80
00:06:57,834 --> 00:07:01,586
A woman's heart is fragile, easily broken
with a spoonful of cheap sympathy.

81
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:05,298
You'd lost feelings a long while ago,
but you still held her hand everywhere.

82
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:09,261
Treated her like a princess!
That's deceit! Deceit is what that is!

83
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:10,345
That's right.

84
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:14,266
What are you going to say next?
That Muhammed Ali got beaten up?

85
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:17,894
What did he do to hear all this
cheap sympathy and deceit nonsense?

86
00:07:17,895 --> 00:07:19,479
- What?
- Hold up.

87
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:21,149
What are you all talking about?

88
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:24,901
What are you talking about?

89
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:26,903
Wait, so it's not like that?

90
00:07:26,904 --> 00:07:28,030
I guess not.

91
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,906
- Well…
- Well, you see…

92
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:32,492
We thought it was like that,
so that's what we told her.

93
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:34,744
We didn't want Eun-sae to end up
being the fool.

94
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:36,663
And what exactly did you tell her?

95
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:38,499
- Well…
- We just…

96
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,919
Tae-ha, you said
you weren't going to marry her.

97
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:45,630
Yeah, that she had no memory
and no place to go,

98
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:47,340
so you let her stay out of pity.

99
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:49,260
That you don't see her that way.

100
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:50,677
Sorry?

101
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:52,762
Isn't that why you two fought yesterday?

102
00:07:52,763 --> 00:07:55,724
Yeong-sil from the pub said so.
That Eun-sae kept saying,

103
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:59,686
"Why did you do all that
when you had no intention of marrying me?"

104
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:00,854
What the…

105
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:02,023
Poor Eun-sae.

106
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:05,318
So she wasn't drinking yesterday
because her memory returned?

107
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:14,034
GUJIN-GUN OFFICE

108
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:17,205
Hello. How can I help you?

109
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:23,127
I'm an unidentified person with no family.

110
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:27,506
I have amnesia, so I don't know who I am.

111
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:28,591
As for my identity…

112
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:32,428
Goodness.

113
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:36,182
I couldn't find it because of this.

114
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:42,396
I want to go to a government facility
that protects people like me.

115
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,398
Darn it.

116
00:08:45,316 --> 00:08:49,611
So this was because you misunderstood,
as did all of you?

117
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:53,241
All of this happened
because of a misunderstanding?

118
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,326
- A misunderstanding?
- A mis…

119
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:57,494
- Misunderstanding?
- How…

120
00:08:57,495 --> 00:08:59,746
Hey, where are you going all of a sudden?

121
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,999
- We need to check the CCTV footage now.
- Right.

122
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:19,016
- There's Eun-sae, getting in a taxi.
- Yeah.

123
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:23,228
Wait.

124
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:25,480
- Isn't that Dal-su's taxi?
- Yeah!

125
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:27,941
Go on, then. Hurry and call Dal-su.

126
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:28,900
Yeah.

127
00:09:28,901 --> 00:09:29,944
Good heavens.

128
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:34,447
Oh boy.

129
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:37,784
Tae-ha, I know it's important
to go and find your wife,

130
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:40,245
but we still have
a lot of life left to live too!

131
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:43,916
I still need to see Pil-seung get married!

132
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:56,344
- Oh, Tae-ha!
- Goodness.

133
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:58,014
- Sir!
- Goodness, Tae-ha!

134
00:10:02,101 --> 00:10:04,854
It's locked. Tae-ha, they're closed.

135
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:10,401
- What's wrong?
- What is it? What?

136
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:11,861
Tae-ha!

137
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:21,996
How'd he do that?

138
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:27,668
If you know Ji-won,
you must know where she is.

139
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:29,753
Where is she?

140
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:31,212
I'll ask you first.

141
00:10:31,213 --> 00:10:33,758
What's your relationship with Ms. Ji-won?

142
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:39,512
You didn't come here knowing everything?

143
00:10:39,513 --> 00:10:40,931
Please answer me first.

144
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:45,519
Ji-won is my girlfriend.

145
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:49,023
She's been missing for over a month.

146
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:51,776
Do you have proof?

147
00:10:57,907 --> 00:10:59,533
Have a scroll through.

148
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:15,633
If the photos aren't proof enough,
you can go to the Prosecutors' Office.

149
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:17,509
- Prosecutors' Office?
- Yes.

150
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:18,803
Prosecutor Go and I…

151
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:23,474
Most of the guards, investigators,
and her fellow prosecutors knew about us.

152
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,270
Prosecutor?

153
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:31,023
Where is Ji-won?

154
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:36,194
Gujin doesn't have any facilities.

155
00:11:36,195 --> 00:11:38,531
They say you have to go
all the way to Dangjin.

156
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:42,033
You'll stay at a temporary
homeless shelter for a few days

157
00:11:42,034 --> 00:11:43,994
before moving to a self-support center.

158
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:47,873
My goodness, to lose your entire memory…

159
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:52,419
Usually, people have at least someone
by their side in situations like these.

160
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,879
Do you really not have anyone?

161
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:06,016
Good grief!

162
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:08,978
Damn it.

163
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:34,043
What the heck was that for?
You can't just do that.

164
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:36,045
You're asking for an accident, you know!

165
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:37,298
I'm her husband.

166
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:46,599
She's not alone.

167
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:48,434
She has me by her side.

168
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:50,478
What?

169
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,438
And she has sisters.

170
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:55,482
And a super obedient little brother.

171
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,151
And a slightly older brother-in-law.

172
00:12:57,651 --> 00:13:00,446
And a friend who transcends age.

173
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:07,286
What's going on here?

174
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:10,246
What is all this?

175
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:13,583
That guy risked all our lives
to come here.

176
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,169
He drove like it was a roller coaster.

177
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:19,255
He even jumped over
the totem-pole-high county office gates.

178
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:21,675
I thought he was going to take flight.

179
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:24,220
Why go to such lengths…

180
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,805
Why do you think?

181
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:29,391
He was worried
that he might lose his wife.

182
00:13:31,018 --> 00:13:32,228
That makes no sense.

183
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:34,647
You told me to go.

184
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:36,315
To leave.

185
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,278
That was all our fault.

186
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:44,531
We shouldn't have gotten involved.

187
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:47,618
Turns out, we made you
misunderstand each other.

188
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,703
Sorry.

189
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,709
You weren't keeping me around
because you pitied me?

190
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:57,670
That dog of yours.

191
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,213
The dog.

192
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,549
He was talking about the dog.

193
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:03,509
You actually believed that?

194
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:06,678
You said you didn't even see me that way.

195
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,930
That was about Su-ji.

196
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:14,353
I'm so nervous I can barely breathe,
even now.

197
00:14:15,312 --> 00:14:17,648
But you said you wouldn't marry me!

198
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:21,694
Because everything you know about us

199
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:24,321
is based on what I told you.

200
00:14:25,489 --> 00:14:26,866
When your memory comes back…

201
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:30,786
If, when your memory returns…

202
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:33,372
If you still

203
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:35,875
feel that way about me…

204
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:38,919
then…

205
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:42,006
give me permission

206
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:44,383
to marry you.

207
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:51,390
Are you serious?

208
00:14:54,643 --> 00:14:56,145
You don't hate me?

209
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:01,692
I can really stay?

210
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:05,279
Go Eun-sae.

211
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:09,450
Let's go

212
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:11,493
home.

213
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:28,302
It really felt like my world was ending.

214
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:31,847
I was fearful of living without you.

215
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:35,267
It felt so much like hell.

216
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:53,035
Silly me. I'm tearing up.

217
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:54,870
Right?

218
00:15:55,537 --> 00:15:58,374
Goodness me.
Why are you crying, young man?

219
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:02,169
I cry whenever I see someone else cry.

220
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,561
I bet their hands are all sweaty.

221
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:43,252
What…

222
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,380
What is all this?

223
00:16:57,891 --> 00:17:01,186
There's a reason we call him
Taffy Village's Choi Soo-jong.

224
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:09,193
- Looks like her.
- Go on, then. Hurry and call Dal-su.

225
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:10,862
- Yeah, okay.
- Goodness.

226
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:13,656
It's a good thing
she got in Dal-su's taxi.

227
00:17:13,657 --> 00:17:15,576
- What is this?
- What's this?

228
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:17,494
What is all this?

229
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,293
Did you order these

230
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:29,256
right after she said she liked
light pink roses yesterday morning?

231
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:39,933
Deceit, my foot.

232
00:17:40,851 --> 00:17:42,394
Darn it.

233
00:17:42,936 --> 00:17:45,731
Let me call Dal-su…

234
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:49,193
<i>Is this because</i>

235
00:17:49,693 --> 00:17:52,112
I said light pink roses are pretty?

236
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:56,325
You like them.

237
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:01,163
Honestly.

238
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,291
You're impossible.

239
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:08,837
I was just talking about a bouquet.

240
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:13,257
There's no middle ground with this guy.

241
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:15,719
As a boxer, he only won gold medals.
No silvers.

242
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,722
Then, at school,
he was always last in his class.

243
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:21,558
Come on, Coach.

244
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:25,645
It's just so pretty.
Why don't you take a picture?

245
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:27,605
Yes! It's so pretty.

246
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:30,733
It's so pretty. You two should dress up
like a bride and groom.

247
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:32,443
And take a picture here.

248
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:33,486
Sounds good.

249
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:34,863
Can we do that?

250
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:36,865
I'd like to take a picture.

251
00:18:40,744 --> 00:18:41,745
Okay.

252
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:47,376
Okay, we'll take the picture now.
The bride and groom.

253
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:50,045
Please hold hands.

254
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:53,965
- What are you waiting for?
- How sweet!

255
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:56,342
Okay, here goes. Three, two, one.

256
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:58,177
- That's it.
- Perfect!

257
00:18:58,178 --> 00:18:59,220
How pretty.

258
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:01,389
Okay, now face each other.

259
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:03,975
- That's it!
- Look at each other.

260
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:06,519
More. Face each other.

261
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:11,399
Now, groom, hold out your hands.
Bride, place your hands on his.

262
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,733
That's nice.

263
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:14,443
Now look at the camera.

264
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:16,738
Three, two, one!

265
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:24,996
- You look lovely.
- Take care.

266
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:27,040
- You look good.
- Take care, sir.

267
00:19:27,666 --> 00:19:28,500
Do well.

268
00:19:29,084 --> 00:19:30,042
Good night.

269
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:31,919
- You too.
- Bye, So-wol.

270
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,462
- See you.
- Good night.

271
00:19:33,463 --> 00:19:35,423
Congratulations? What is this, a wedding?

272
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:36,549
Honestly.

273
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:38,093
- Good night.
- One second.

274
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:42,305
Now the misunderstanding
has all been cleared up,

275
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:44,140
and this young man won't be around,

276
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:46,726
which means tonight
is your first night alone.

277
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:47,853
Goodness gracious!

278
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:52,565
I hope you don't wake up the whole village
in the middle of the night.

279
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:54,317
You're absolutely crazy.

280
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:57,195
Tae-ha, what makes a man?
Confidence, okay?

281
00:19:57,196 --> 00:20:00,031
On a night like tonight,
a bed isn't a piece of furniture.

282
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:01,365
It's a stage.

283
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:03,326
In bed, a man must be confident!

284
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:06,621
Please stop.
We'll take care of it ourselves.

285
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:08,623
- Yourselves?
- They'll take care of it?

286
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:09,666
Themselves?

287
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:11,334
Please hurry home.

288
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:13,045
- Get home safe.
- Goodbye.

289
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:17,883
I don't know why they're like that.

290
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:34,523
Well…

291
00:20:34,524 --> 00:20:36,318
Yeah, well…

292
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:41,530
Shall we…

293
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,450
Shall we have a drink?

294
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:51,917
Wow, you had something like this?

295
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:55,002
You must be a total drinker,

296
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:57,965
carrying something like this around
and drinking by yourself.

297
00:20:58,924 --> 00:20:59,800
You drank with me.

298
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:03,637
I did? When?

299
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:07,432
In Japan. Under the cherry blossoms.

300
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:10,185
Cherry blossoms?

301
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:14,439
This place is so beautiful.

302
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:20,821
It must have been so romantic.

303
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:24,740
I want my memory to return soon.

304
00:21:24,741 --> 00:21:28,704
It's so unfair that you're the only one
who remembers all of that good stuff.

305
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:38,839
Perfect.

306
00:21:47,097 --> 00:21:48,765
By the way,

307
00:21:49,766 --> 00:21:52,769
what was it about what I said
that you misunderstood?

308
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:56,772
What?

309
00:21:56,773 --> 00:22:01,445
The harsh things you said to me earlier
sounded so real.

310
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:03,196
It scared me a little.

311
00:22:09,202 --> 00:22:11,955
The time we spent together
in Taffy Village…

312
00:22:13,582 --> 00:22:14,458
I thought

313
00:22:15,917 --> 00:22:17,419
you hated it all.

314
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:21,423
There's no way.

315
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:32,100
Someday, when time passes
and your memory returns,

316
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:36,480
and even if the day comes
when you don't like me anymore,

317
00:22:38,357 --> 00:22:39,483
I hope our time together

318
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:42,903
won't be a painful memory for you.

319
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:52,871
You really like me, don't you?

320
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:56,083
Worrying about things you don't need to.

321
00:22:57,667 --> 00:23:00,796
There's no way I'd ever not like you.

322
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:07,302
But why do you like me so much?

323
00:23:08,553 --> 00:23:12,223
- You're p--
- Don't say it's because I'm pretty.

324
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:13,350
That's so cliché.

325
00:23:15,769 --> 00:23:17,854
I was going to say
it's because you're polite.

326
00:23:20,732 --> 00:23:21,566
What?

327
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:23,693
Say that again.

328
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:26,363
You're actually quite polite,

329
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,615
subtly taking care of Grandma.

330
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:30,659
And up until a moment ago,

331
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,703
you spoke formally to me.

332
00:23:37,749 --> 00:23:40,209
Seriously, stop joking around.

333
00:23:40,210 --> 00:23:43,003
Tell me why you really like me. Now.

334
00:23:43,004 --> 00:23:43,839
I don't know.

335
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:50,428
Come on, you really have nothing to say?

336
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,347
I really don't know. I just

337
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:54,224
don't like other women.

338
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:01,356
When I'm with you, I get…

339
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:04,443
a little weird.

340
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:14,202
You know what?

341
00:24:15,454 --> 00:24:16,746
I'm like that too.

342
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:20,500
I get nervous, too,

343
00:24:21,084 --> 00:24:22,752
when I'm with you.

344
00:24:25,922 --> 00:24:27,382
I can barely breathe.

345
00:24:35,015 --> 00:24:37,766
Now I like you more than Cha Eun-woo.

346
00:24:37,767 --> 00:24:42,104
And the password to my new email
is "Jang Tae-ha."

347
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:44,940
The first face that comes to mind
when I wake up,

348
00:24:44,941 --> 00:24:49,362
and the last face that comes to mind
before I go to sleep, is Jang Tae-ha's.

349
00:24:56,703 --> 00:24:57,954
I like you.

350
00:25:03,084 --> 00:25:04,377
A lot.

351
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:40,764
Gi-jun, what brings you here--

352
00:26:40,765 --> 00:26:42,392
What the hell are you up to?

353
00:26:43,476 --> 00:26:45,144
- What?
- I know everything.

354
00:26:45,145 --> 00:26:47,063
Who she really is, who you've been hiding.

355
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:52,736
Anti-corruption Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Seoul Prosecutors' Office.

356
00:26:55,155 --> 00:26:56,489
Tell me.

357
00:26:57,574 --> 00:26:58,408
How did you know?

358
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:01,036
I just met with Gwak Chi-hyeon.

359
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:04,997
Go Eun-sae… I mean, Prosecutor Go Ji-won.
He's looking for her.

360
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:08,168
How do you know about him?
How much did you tell him?

361
00:27:09,085 --> 00:27:11,545
- Did you tell him that she's here?
- Answer me first.

362
00:27:11,546 --> 00:27:14,215
What happened?
Do you know that this is a crime?

363
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:25,435
Gi-jun, let's talk for a second.

364
00:27:29,689 --> 00:27:32,484
I need to meet Chairman Baek.

365
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:47,916
So, you saved Go Eun-sae
when you were supposed to kill her,

366
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:51,670
and you pretended to be her boyfriend
to keep her safe.

367
00:27:52,629 --> 00:27:55,881
And because she would only agree to flee
if she regained her memory,

368
00:27:55,882 --> 00:27:57,676
you were sincere about her treatment.

369
00:27:58,259 --> 00:27:59,094
Is that right?

370
00:28:03,223 --> 00:28:05,516
So they really, you know,

371
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:10,188
make you… kill people and stuff?

372
00:28:12,565 --> 00:28:15,568
The man you met, Gwak Chi-hyeon,
is one of Baek Sang-gil's men.

373
00:28:16,361 --> 00:28:19,656
If he knows that she's alive,
he'll probably tell Baek Sang-gil.

374
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:26,121
Now tell me.

375
00:28:27,747 --> 00:28:29,457
How much did you tell Gwak Chi-hyeon?

376
00:28:35,338 --> 00:28:36,506
Everything?

377
00:28:37,632 --> 00:28:38,466
Well…

378
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:44,013
I don't even know why I did that.

379
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:48,935
Where is Ji-won?

380
00:28:57,861 --> 00:28:59,528
I think I'm in the wrong place.

381
00:28:59,529 --> 00:29:00,488
Sorry?

382
00:29:01,197 --> 00:29:03,949
The Go Ji-won I know is not this person.

383
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:05,994
What is this all of a sudden?

384
00:29:08,288 --> 00:29:11,374
This Go Ji-won… I mean, another Go Ji-won

385
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:14,793
has caused a lot of harm
to a lot of people.

386
00:29:14,794 --> 00:29:16,837
So I was looking for her,

387
00:29:16,838 --> 00:29:19,424
but it seems they just share
the same name.

388
00:29:20,925 --> 00:29:23,094
Then how did you get my number?

389
00:29:25,180 --> 00:29:26,347
Well,

390
00:29:27,307 --> 00:29:31,685
I had someone look into
Go Ji-won's acquaintances,

391
00:29:31,686 --> 00:29:35,690
but I think the private investigator
made a mistake.

392
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:43,697
Anyway, I don't know this person.
I apologize for the inconvenience.

393
00:29:43,698 --> 00:29:45,325
Wait. Excuse me?

394
00:29:48,953 --> 00:29:52,915
You and I were never that close,

395
00:29:52,916 --> 00:29:57,628
and we were polar opposites,
the top student and the bottom student.

396
00:29:57,629 --> 00:30:00,089
But I know you're not a bad guy.

397
00:30:00,673 --> 00:30:03,926
I wanted to hear you out first

398
00:30:03,927 --> 00:30:07,347
before deciding whether to hand her over
to Gwak Chi-hyeon or call the cops.

399
00:30:08,348 --> 00:30:09,682
Right, thanks.

400
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:11,976
I really mean it. Thanks, Gi-jun.

401
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:14,771
No problem.

402
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:16,981
But

403
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:21,528
if Go Eun-sae never gets her memory back,

404
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:23,571
what are you going to do?

405
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:29,118
I'll have to force her to leave.

406
00:30:29,869 --> 00:30:31,037
But if I do that,

407
00:30:32,247 --> 00:30:33,957
Go Eun-sae will be devastated.

408
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:36,960
I actually meant to ask.

409
00:30:37,460 --> 00:30:40,630
Is there really no way
to get her memory back faster?

410
00:30:42,632 --> 00:30:45,342
The treatment's already brought back
some of her memory.

411
00:30:45,343 --> 00:30:47,387
Like her remembering Gwak Chi-hyeon.

412
00:30:48,471 --> 00:30:49,513
From now on,

413
00:30:49,514 --> 00:30:55,353
you need to help her see, feel,
and experience things from her past

414
00:30:55,937 --> 00:30:58,064
to trigger any memories related to them.

415
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:05,904
I've been dying to ask you.

416
00:31:05,905 --> 00:31:09,826
What's with all these flowers?

417
00:31:10,827 --> 00:31:11,661
What?

418
00:31:14,539 --> 00:31:15,665
Oh, these?

419
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:19,836
Go Eun-sae said roses are pretty.

420
00:31:21,170 --> 00:31:22,338
And women,

421
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:25,091
they like this sort of thing?

422
00:31:26,593 --> 00:31:27,719
What?

423
00:31:30,847 --> 00:31:31,764
Never mind.

424
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:33,766
I'm going.

425
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:35,101
Okay.

426
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:39,564
Can I take one of these?

427
00:31:40,064 --> 00:31:42,483
Yeah, sure. You can take a lot.

428
00:31:42,984 --> 00:31:45,570
These roses are unique.

429
00:32:02,462 --> 00:32:03,755
That bastard.

430
00:32:04,714 --> 00:32:06,132
He's so damn cool.

431
00:32:07,634 --> 00:32:09,093
- Trouble?
- Yes.

432
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:13,805
I keep thinking that Prosecutor Go
might have gotten into some trouble.

433
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:16,558
If today was about sending someone
to test the waters,

434
00:32:16,559 --> 00:32:19,144
he should have asked me something.

435
00:32:19,145 --> 00:32:21,814
But he didn't ask me anything significant.

436
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,566
What are the chances
of a true coincidence?

437
00:32:24,567 --> 00:32:29,113
No, he definitely reacted
to the photos of Prosecutor Go.

438
00:32:33,076 --> 00:32:34,701
She got into some trouble…

439
00:32:34,702 --> 00:32:39,540
Maybe she got seriously injured
or was kidnapped by someone.

440
00:32:41,292 --> 00:32:43,378
That's why I came to see you, sir.

441
00:32:45,254 --> 00:32:49,050
Please trace the phone number
of the man I met today.

442
00:32:49,717 --> 00:32:52,553
I'm sure he is somehow connected
to Prosecutor Go.

443
00:32:58,559 --> 00:33:01,354
Come on.

444
00:33:02,313 --> 00:33:04,106
On such an important night,

445
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:08,318
why did I have to go and get wasted
and fall asleep?

446
00:33:08,319 --> 00:33:10,697
Stupid.

447
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:25,252
That's right.

448
00:33:25,253 --> 00:33:26,462
Last night.

449
00:33:26,963 --> 00:33:29,548
I remember
the atmosphere was really tense.

450
00:33:29,549 --> 00:33:31,592
Why would the two of them be like that?

451
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,599
Did they fight over me?

452
00:33:40,518 --> 00:33:41,601
What am I going to do?

453
00:33:41,602 --> 00:33:42,729
You're up?

454
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:45,230
Jang Tae-ha.

455
00:33:45,231 --> 00:33:47,191
Doctor An came by last night, didn't he?

456
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:49,861
Yes.

457
00:33:50,737 --> 00:33:52,070
How did you know?

458
00:33:52,071 --> 00:33:54,657
I thought I saw him
when I briefly woke up.

459
00:33:58,244 --> 00:34:00,495
Don't worry too much.

460
00:34:00,496 --> 00:34:02,665
I'll give him a serious talking-to.

461
00:34:06,502 --> 00:34:08,128
WE UNDERSTAND YOUR FEELINGS

462
00:34:08,129 --> 00:34:09,881
Lean back comfortably for a bit.

463
00:34:11,591 --> 00:34:14,052
I'm not comfortable
because of you, Doctor.

464
00:34:14,635 --> 00:34:15,552
Sorry?

465
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:19,514
I think I should say this
before we start the treatment.

466
00:34:19,515 --> 00:34:22,143
Since you came all the way
to our home last night.

467
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:25,771
I know we've gotten a lot closer recently.

468
00:34:25,772 --> 00:34:29,441
I got drunk, and you carried me home.

469
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:31,486
I must have made a scene.

470
00:34:32,111 --> 00:34:33,445
But that wasn't a sign

471
00:34:33,446 --> 00:34:37,658
that you could cross the line.

472
00:34:39,327 --> 00:34:41,579
I'm in a common-law marriage.

473
00:34:42,538 --> 00:34:45,874
We haven't had a wedding yet,
but we're practically married.

474
00:34:45,875 --> 00:34:47,668
And I really,

475
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:50,046
really like Jang Tae-ha.

476
00:34:50,546 --> 00:34:52,380
So I'm sorry,

477
00:34:52,381 --> 00:34:55,343
but I hope we can remain

478
00:34:55,927 --> 00:34:59,555
as a doctor and a patient.

479
00:35:00,515 --> 00:35:03,183
What is this nonsense?
Did you drink again?

480
00:35:03,184 --> 00:35:04,101
What?

481
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,352
Wow, this is…

482
00:35:05,353 --> 00:35:07,313
This is bad. My goodness.

483
00:35:07,814 --> 00:35:09,189
Where do I even start? Okay.

484
00:35:09,190 --> 00:35:11,900
I'm sorry, but Ms. Go Eun-sae,

485
00:35:11,901 --> 00:35:13,402
you're not my type.

486
00:35:14,570 --> 00:35:16,738
I like women who look pure and innocent

487
00:35:16,739 --> 00:35:19,407
and have eyes
that point to twenty past eight.

488
00:35:19,408 --> 00:35:22,035
But looking at you now,

489
00:35:22,036 --> 00:35:24,955
your eyes are more… thirteen past nine.

490
00:35:24,956 --> 00:35:29,127
And what's more,
I don't like women who are too tall.

491
00:35:29,877 --> 00:35:31,378
I have a bad neck, so…

492
00:35:31,379 --> 00:35:34,256
Then why did you suddenly come to see
Jang Tae-ha last night

493
00:35:34,257 --> 00:35:36,800
and look up at him
like you were picking a fight?

494
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:38,677
Hey, I did not look up at him!

495
00:35:38,678 --> 00:35:40,971
We were totally eye to eye!

496
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:43,682
You were looking up at him like this!

497
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:45,350
Ms. Eun-sae, sit down, okay?

498
00:35:45,351 --> 00:35:47,270
- Wait a second.
- You're here for treatment.

499
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:53,317
I'm done. Let's go.

500
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:56,487
Have a safe trip home.

501
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:02,200
<i>I like women who look pure and innocent</i>

502
00:36:02,201 --> 00:36:04,704
<i>and have eyes
that point to twenty past eight.</i>

503
00:36:12,086 --> 00:36:13,337
Just put something down.

504
00:36:14,213 --> 00:36:15,630
- Just wait.
- Oh, come on!

505
00:36:15,631 --> 00:36:17,048
- Seriously?
- Did you see that?

506
00:36:17,049 --> 00:36:18,259
- How the heck?
- Here goes!

507
00:36:18,759 --> 00:36:20,635
What even is this?

508
00:36:20,636 --> 00:36:22,804
A double sweep. Cough up two cards each.

509
00:36:22,805 --> 00:36:24,598
Come on!

510
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:27,309
All the top cards are going to you today.

511
00:36:27,310 --> 00:36:30,604
And you got all the double junk cards.
It's your lucky day.

512
00:36:30,605 --> 00:36:32,230
Tell me about it.

513
00:36:32,231 --> 00:36:35,609
I wonder what good thing
is going to happen to me…

514
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:37,320
Should I buy a lottery ticket?

515
00:36:38,029 --> 00:36:39,196
I avoided the penalty.

516
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:41,073
Isn't that Pil-seung?

517
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:42,824
Oh my.

518
00:36:42,825 --> 00:36:46,954
He's marching over here like Lee Jung-jae
in <i>The Face Reader</i>.

519
00:37:00,426 --> 00:37:01,801
Let's go. Come on.

520
00:37:01,802 --> 00:37:02,802
Wait, Mom.

521
00:37:02,803 --> 00:37:03,970
Oh, shut it.

522
00:37:03,971 --> 00:37:05,472
Mom, please.

523
00:37:05,473 --> 00:37:08,350
Why does it have to be fist fights?

524
00:37:08,351 --> 00:37:12,646
I raised you for 17 years, making sure
you never got a single scratch.

525
00:37:12,647 --> 00:37:15,732
And now you want me
to watch some scary punks

526
00:37:15,733 --> 00:37:16,816
whack you on the head?

527
00:37:16,817 --> 00:37:19,028
I won't get whacked. I'll hit them harder.

528
00:37:21,113 --> 00:37:24,909
All right. Let's say you do well
and even win a medal.

529
00:37:25,826 --> 00:37:29,621
What will you do after you retire?
Who'd hire a guy who fought for a living?

530
00:37:29,622 --> 00:37:33,751
People will just call you empty-headed
wherever you go.

531
00:37:34,252 --> 00:37:36,586
- What if I fill my head?
- What's this now?

532
00:37:36,587 --> 00:37:40,340
If I'm good at boxing and get smart,
no one will be able to say that.

533
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:41,967
You're going to study?

534
00:37:41,968 --> 00:37:44,552
You're the last in your whole school.

535
00:37:44,553 --> 00:37:47,138
If I do well on the next mock exam,
let me box.

536
00:37:47,139 --> 00:37:48,766
<i>Is that a deal or not?</i>

537
00:37:51,227 --> 00:37:52,144
What's wrong?

538
00:37:54,272 --> 00:37:55,523
Why are you… A report card?

539
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:57,983
- A report card?
- It's Pil-seung's.

540
00:37:57,984 --> 00:37:59,150
What place…

541
00:37:59,151 --> 00:38:01,361
Fifth… in the whole school.

542
00:38:01,362 --> 00:38:02,487
Fifth in your school?

543
00:38:02,488 --> 00:38:04,406
Pil-seung! Goodness, Hui-ja!

544
00:38:04,407 --> 00:38:08,159
There's no doubt about it.
It's five, just like five top cards!

545
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:08,995
Five!

546
00:38:14,709 --> 00:38:16,627
Fine, you can box.

547
00:38:18,879 --> 00:38:22,590
You must have really wanted this
if you went from last to fifth place.

548
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:24,593
I'm going to the nationals
in two days' time.

549
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:28,680
But

550
00:38:28,681 --> 00:38:32,225
can you go there just like that?

551
00:38:32,226 --> 00:38:33,477
I applied three months ago.

552
00:38:34,437 --> 00:38:36,063
I planned on competing anyway.

553
00:38:36,564 --> 00:38:40,400
But you haven't been able to train
because you've been studying.

554
00:38:40,401 --> 00:38:42,820
No. I haven't taken
a single day off from training.

555
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:05,759
<i>Other than eating and pooping,</i>

556
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:08,387
<i>I studied and trained
as if my life depended on it.</i>

557
00:39:08,929 --> 00:39:10,138
<i>Now that you know,</i>

558
00:39:10,139 --> 00:39:12,183
I thought I'd be up front
and ask permission.

559
00:39:17,271 --> 00:39:18,105
Okay.

560
00:39:18,606 --> 00:39:21,399
A promise is a promise.
You can compete in that thingy.

561
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:22,485
You mean that?

562
00:39:23,069 --> 00:39:24,028
But

563
00:39:25,196 --> 00:39:26,030
I'm not going.

564
00:39:27,406 --> 00:39:32,078
I can't bear to see someone
whacking you in the head.

565
00:39:33,871 --> 00:39:35,790
Don't make me sit through that too.

566
00:39:38,501 --> 00:39:39,627
Please look after him.

567
00:39:41,045 --> 00:39:42,171
Mrs. Pang…

568
00:39:48,552 --> 00:39:51,639
I heard that Prosecutor Go Ji-won is alive

569
00:39:52,932 --> 00:39:55,726
and that she's holding a knife
to our throats.

570
00:39:57,019 --> 00:39:58,603
How did you find out about that?

571
00:39:58,604 --> 00:40:00,980
Did you really think
that when my previous aide

572
00:40:00,981 --> 00:40:06,028
made a mess and still survived you,
I wouldn't have him tailed?

573
00:40:07,696 --> 00:40:08,655
Well, well.

574
00:40:08,656 --> 00:40:10,699
I didn't know
our mayor was capable of that.

575
00:40:11,367 --> 00:40:14,577
I wonder why someone in silk robes
would dirty themselves with mud.

576
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:16,539
Then you should have cleaned up properly!

577
00:40:19,625 --> 00:40:22,710
You couldn't even handle
a rookie nobody prosecutor

578
00:40:22,711 --> 00:40:23,921
and left crumbs behind?

579
00:40:24,797 --> 00:40:25,714
Makes me uneasy.

580
00:40:27,716 --> 00:40:31,053
The party is all in, building me up
as a presidential candidate.

581
00:40:32,012 --> 00:40:33,096
Momentum's good.

582
00:40:33,097 --> 00:40:36,183
I'm close to moving into the house
adorned with the rose of Sharon.

583
00:40:36,767 --> 00:40:37,684
Don't sully it.

584
00:40:37,685 --> 00:40:41,355
I buried 11 corpses
under the roots of that rose of Sharon.

585
00:40:43,983 --> 00:40:48,279
If I, Baek Sang-gil, were to become
a mad dog and dig up that land…

586
00:40:51,073 --> 00:40:53,117
they'd all come out into the open.

587
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,661
Could you handle that?

588
00:40:59,248 --> 00:41:00,331
So,

589
00:41:00,332 --> 00:41:02,876
let's not waste time
barking at each other.

590
00:41:02,877 --> 00:41:06,464
I'm looking for her,
and I won't let anything go wrong.

591
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:15,763
- I'll be going now, Coach.
- Yeah, good work.

592
00:41:15,764 --> 00:41:17,640
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

593
00:41:17,641 --> 00:41:19,268
- Get home safe.
- You got it!

594
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:24,230
Pil-seung is awesome.

595
00:41:24,231 --> 00:41:26,317
So youthful spirit wins everything.

596
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:28,318
Oh, right!

597
00:41:28,319 --> 00:41:30,945
I want to go cheer for Pil-seung
at his match.

598
00:41:30,946 --> 00:41:32,531
It's too dangerous to leave…

599
00:41:33,407 --> 00:41:39,371
<i>You need to help her see, feel,
and experience things from her past.</i>

600
00:41:40,539 --> 00:41:42,333
Okay, let's go together.

601
00:41:42,917 --> 00:41:44,919
Really? Yay!

602
00:41:48,130 --> 00:41:50,257
That one. Is that yours?

603
00:41:51,842 --> 00:41:54,553
Yeah, it's a medal I got back
thanks to my first love.

604
00:41:56,514 --> 00:41:59,183
Why are you bringing up
your first love right now?

605
00:42:09,527 --> 00:42:11,654
Do you want to hit this if you're angry?

606
00:42:15,199 --> 00:42:18,577
Mention your first love again and see
what happens. I'm the jealous type.

607
00:42:19,703 --> 00:42:23,290
By the way, I was in your room yesterday.
It's so drafty in there.

608
00:42:24,500 --> 00:42:25,334
No, it's not.

609
00:42:25,834 --> 00:42:26,961
Yes, it is.

610
00:42:27,628 --> 00:42:31,298
Why don't you sleep in my room from now on
so you don't catch a cold?

611
00:42:33,092 --> 00:42:34,927
Is that all you think about?

612
00:42:35,427 --> 00:42:39,097
Yes, of course.
I only think about you all day long.

613
00:42:39,098 --> 00:42:40,891
We're not sharing a bed.

614
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:44,602
And why not?

615
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:46,855
I told you. You make me nervous.

616
00:42:47,356 --> 00:42:48,816
I need to prepare myself.

617
00:42:54,905 --> 00:42:56,072
Fine.

618
00:42:56,073 --> 00:43:00,493
Then I'll give you a few days
to prepare yourself.

619
00:43:00,494 --> 00:43:02,870
I think I've gained some weight recently,

620
00:43:02,871 --> 00:43:04,373
so I should get back in shape.

621
00:43:05,082 --> 00:43:05,916
You haven't.

622
00:43:06,709 --> 00:43:07,710
You're pretty.

623
00:43:09,086 --> 00:43:10,670
So you know the right answer.

624
00:43:10,671 --> 00:43:12,840
Quite a master at flirting, aren't you?

625
00:43:13,507 --> 00:43:15,717
Be honest.
You've dated a lot, haven't you?

626
00:43:15,718 --> 00:43:17,844
- I haven't.
- As if.

627
00:43:17,845 --> 00:43:20,930
I'll forgive you if you tell me now.
But you have to tell me now.

628
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:22,057
Be honest.

629
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:40,241
THE 107TH NATIONAL SPORTS FESTIVAL
HIGH SCHOOL BOXING MATCH

630
00:43:40,242 --> 00:43:42,244
We need to get the confetti ready.

631
00:43:47,666 --> 00:43:48,500
BOXING ARENA

632
00:43:55,758 --> 00:43:56,717
Ladies!

633
00:43:57,301 --> 00:43:59,844
- There you are.
- Over here.

634
00:43:59,845 --> 00:44:02,764
- We're coming.
- What is all this?

635
00:44:02,765 --> 00:44:04,223
This is amazing!

636
00:44:04,224 --> 00:44:08,061
We're Pil-seung's aunties
who even changed his diapers.

637
00:44:08,062 --> 00:44:10,688
- This is the least we can do.
- Yeah.

638
00:44:10,689 --> 00:44:13,608
In case folks look down on him
for being from the country.

639
00:44:13,609 --> 00:44:15,818
Who would look down on him
after seeing this?

640
00:44:15,819 --> 00:44:18,321
We're like some kind of gang right now.

641
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:19,823
Oh, come on.

642
00:44:20,908 --> 00:44:23,576
Pil-seung is coming out.
I think it's starting.

643
00:44:23,577 --> 00:44:24,786
There! Pil-seung!

644
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:25,870
The pride of Gujin!

645
00:44:25,871 --> 00:44:28,748
- Kim Pil-seung, go get them!
- You've got this!

646
00:44:28,749 --> 00:44:30,209
Go, Pil-seung!

647
00:44:31,418 --> 00:44:33,086
- It's starting.
- Tae-ha.

648
00:44:33,087 --> 00:44:34,421
Look at me. Are you nervous?

649
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:36,256
Do your best.

650
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:43,597
- Pil-seung has…
- Taffy fists!

651
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:57,069
KO! Red corner wins by KO!

652
00:44:58,987 --> 00:45:00,447
ROUND OF 16

653
00:45:01,365 --> 00:45:06,704
OH SEUNG-HYEON VS KIM PIL-SEUNG

654
00:45:07,538 --> 00:45:08,956
QUARTERFINALS

655
00:45:09,790 --> 00:45:16,797
JUNG GANG-SAN VS KIM PIL-SEUNG

656
00:45:19,591 --> 00:45:20,967
SEMIFINALS

657
00:45:20,968 --> 00:45:25,431
JOO YEONG-MIN VS KIM PIL-SEUNG

658
00:45:29,810 --> 00:45:31,645
That's it! Back away now.

659
00:45:38,068 --> 00:45:39,193
FINAL

660
00:45:39,194 --> 00:45:42,071
GUJIN HIGH, KIM PIL-SEUNG
VS YONGDEOK HIGH, CHOI WON-UK

661
00:45:42,072 --> 00:45:45,033
<i>The high school boxing final
will begin shortly.</i>

662
00:45:47,327 --> 00:45:49,455
Pil-seung, this is the last match.

663
00:45:50,164 --> 00:45:50,998
You've done great.

664
00:45:51,707 --> 00:45:53,040
Don't get nervous

665
00:45:53,041 --> 00:45:55,335
and stay focused until the end, okay?

666
00:45:58,630 --> 00:45:59,631
Let's go!

667
00:46:07,639 --> 00:46:08,766
Swing your arms!

668
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:11,018
More!

669
00:46:16,106 --> 00:46:17,065
That's it! Again!

670
00:46:28,368 --> 00:46:29,745
Get off him.

671
00:46:40,923 --> 00:46:42,007
Damn it!

672
00:46:42,674 --> 00:46:44,134
Excuse me. Please move aside!

673
00:46:47,095 --> 00:46:47,930
Hold on.

674
00:46:51,517 --> 00:46:54,102
Pil-seung, are you okay?

675
00:46:56,146 --> 00:46:57,940
Oh no, what do we do?

676
00:46:59,858 --> 00:47:02,402
Don't you even maintain
the facilities here?

677
00:47:02,986 --> 00:47:06,573
Oh dear. This isn't the kind of bleeding
that will stop anytime soon.

678
00:47:07,324 --> 00:47:10,535
It looks pretty serious,
so we should end the match now.

679
00:47:10,536 --> 00:47:13,079
Let's rule it a loss by decision
for Kim Pil-seung.

680
00:47:13,080 --> 00:47:14,163
No, you can't!

681
00:47:14,164 --> 00:47:15,248
You can't do that.

682
00:47:15,249 --> 00:47:16,958
You should reschedule the match!

683
00:47:16,959 --> 00:47:18,209
According to the rules,

684
00:47:18,210 --> 00:47:22,047
it's up to me, the TD, to decide
whether to reschedule or rule it a loss.

685
00:47:22,631 --> 00:47:24,674
So reschedule the match.

686
00:47:24,675 --> 00:47:26,759
We can do it some other day!

687
00:47:26,760 --> 00:47:29,178
Come on, you know how it is.

688
00:47:29,179 --> 00:47:33,224
Don't you know how complicated it is
to reschedule a match?

689
00:47:33,225 --> 00:47:35,477
Then you'd be happy for us
to take legal action?

690
00:47:36,603 --> 00:47:39,355
- Sorry?
- It's in Article 2 of the Civil Act.

691
00:47:39,356 --> 00:47:41,148
The organizers of a sports event

692
00:47:41,149 --> 00:47:44,777
have a duty, in good faith,
to protect athletes during a competition.

693
00:47:44,778 --> 00:47:48,614
In this case, not only was the athlete
injured due to the organizers' negligence,

694
00:47:48,615 --> 00:47:50,992
he now risks losing his chance at gold.

695
00:47:50,993 --> 00:47:51,951
You tell them!

696
00:47:51,952 --> 00:47:54,078
If this isn't resolved properly,

697
00:47:54,079 --> 00:47:58,541
we will file a lawsuit for breach of duty
regarding injury and medical treatment.

698
00:47:58,542 --> 00:48:00,377
- That's right!
- Yes, a lawsuit!

699
00:48:05,841 --> 00:48:08,886
Then please wait
in the waiting room for now.

700
00:48:09,636 --> 00:48:12,054
- What the heck?
- What are you playing at?

701
00:48:12,055 --> 00:48:14,056
How long do you expect us to wait?

702
00:48:14,057 --> 00:48:15,266
Is he okay?

703
00:48:15,267 --> 00:48:16,726
Pil-seung, are you okay?

704
00:48:16,727 --> 00:48:18,519
- How is it?
- Can I take a look?

705
00:48:18,520 --> 00:48:20,021
He's bleeding too much.

706
00:48:20,022 --> 00:48:22,983
- Oh dear. What if it scars?
- This is so upsetting.

707
00:48:26,820 --> 00:48:28,487
By the way,

708
00:48:28,488 --> 00:48:31,240
how did you know so much
about the law earlier?

709
00:48:31,241 --> 00:48:32,575
Yeah, exactly.

710
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:35,078
- You sounded like a judge or a prosecutor.
- Yeah.

711
00:48:35,787 --> 00:48:37,121
That's what I'm saying.

712
00:48:37,122 --> 00:48:40,042
I don't know how,
but the words just flew out of my mouth.

713
00:48:40,542 --> 00:48:43,921
Before I lost my memory,
maybe I was a pro…

714
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:50,260
- A pro…
- A pro what?

715
00:48:52,679 --> 00:48:53,639
A pro…

716
00:48:54,723 --> 00:48:56,682
A prodigy!

717
00:48:56,683 --> 00:48:58,476
- You <i>were</i> amazing.
- You're smart.

718
00:48:58,477 --> 00:48:59,770
You're amazing.

719
00:49:00,520 --> 00:49:01,479
Or properly scary.

720
00:49:01,480 --> 00:49:03,106
- Surprising, yeah?
- She's smart.

721
00:49:04,942 --> 00:49:06,984
I want the rematch today.

722
00:49:06,985 --> 00:49:08,069
You…

723
00:49:08,070 --> 00:49:09,946
- You're in no state to--
- I can do it.

724
00:49:09,947 --> 00:49:12,616
I don't want a silver medal.
I'll do the rematch today.

725
00:49:15,118 --> 00:49:16,286
Please let him do that.

726
00:49:17,079 --> 00:49:20,122
The bleeding has almost stopped,
and an athlete knows his body best.

727
00:49:20,123 --> 00:49:23,710
The flow of the match was good today,
so Pil-seung must have a good feeling.

728
00:49:30,676 --> 00:49:33,762
BOXING ASSOCIATION OF KOREA
NO ENTRY

729
00:49:36,932 --> 00:49:38,684
Hey!

730
00:49:41,520 --> 00:49:43,562
We told you to go back for now.

731
00:49:43,563 --> 00:49:45,648
The referees and officials
are discussing it,

732
00:49:45,649 --> 00:49:48,276
so if you wait in the waiting room,
we'll let you know.

733
00:49:49,987 --> 00:49:51,320
Hey!

734
00:49:51,321 --> 00:49:56,159
I won't put a silver medal
around my boy's neck like this!

735
00:49:56,660 --> 00:49:59,371
Even if he gets a silver medal,

736
00:49:59,871 --> 00:50:02,207
it happens today, you hear?

737
00:50:02,708 --> 00:50:03,624
Please!

738
00:50:03,625 --> 00:50:07,379
<i>Let him fight today in his gloves
for whatever medal!</i>

739
00:50:08,046 --> 00:50:09,296
<i>Okay?</i>

740
00:50:09,297 --> 00:50:11,008
<i>Are you listening?</i>

741
00:50:13,301 --> 00:50:14,344
<i>You hear?</i>

742
00:50:20,225 --> 00:50:21,059
How did it go?

743
00:50:23,603 --> 00:50:24,438
Have a seat.

744
00:50:33,447 --> 00:50:34,281
Are you sure

745
00:50:35,490 --> 00:50:36,575
you're up for it?

746
00:50:40,829 --> 00:50:41,663
Okay.

747
00:50:42,414 --> 00:50:43,373
Pil-seung.

748
00:50:44,291 --> 00:50:45,125
It's okay to lose.

749
00:50:47,002 --> 00:50:51,047
For not giving up
and keeping your gloves on until the end,

750
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:53,508
you've already won gold in my eyes.

751
00:51:04,478 --> 00:51:06,104
I have a favor to ask.

752
00:51:07,939 --> 00:51:09,357
Just don't get hurt.

753
00:51:18,617 --> 00:51:20,660
FINAL
KIM PIL-SEUNG VS CHOI WON-UK

754
00:51:22,329 --> 00:51:23,412
Please.

755
00:51:23,413 --> 00:51:25,916
- Pil-seung.
- Pil-seung, you've got this!

756
00:51:30,295 --> 00:51:31,420
Come on, Pil-seung!

757
00:51:31,421 --> 00:51:32,255
Go, taffy fists!

758
00:51:36,635 --> 00:51:37,844
That's it.

759
00:51:38,804 --> 00:51:40,054
Yeah, that's it.

760
00:51:40,055 --> 00:51:42,390
- Circle more.
- Keep moving!

761
00:51:43,183 --> 00:51:44,226
Get closer!

762
00:51:48,563 --> 00:51:49,939
- Oh my!
- Do it!

763
00:51:49,940 --> 00:51:52,317
- Stay on him! Corner him!
- Lead hand.

764
00:51:57,155 --> 00:51:59,199
- Oh no!
- Guard up.

765
00:52:06,706 --> 00:52:08,125
Red, back to your corner.

766
00:52:23,598 --> 00:52:25,058
Red corner wins by KO!

767
00:52:27,686 --> 00:52:29,228
Pil-seung, good job!

768
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:31,230
Great job, Pil-seung!

769
00:52:31,231 --> 00:52:32,439
Come here.

770
00:52:32,440 --> 00:52:33,775
Good job!

771
00:52:34,276 --> 00:52:36,153
Pil-seung, you did great!

772
00:52:49,374 --> 00:52:51,001
You did well. You were great.

773
00:52:51,501 --> 00:52:52,544
You did great.

774
00:52:53,170 --> 00:52:55,796
Great work. Congratulations on gold.

775
00:52:55,797 --> 00:52:56,882
Coach!

776
00:53:00,385 --> 00:53:01,845
Wait one second.

777
00:53:26,244 --> 00:53:28,830
Why are you crying? I won.

778
00:53:33,668 --> 00:53:35,920
This is why!

779
00:53:35,921 --> 00:53:40,592
This is why I didn't want you to fight.

780
00:53:41,426 --> 00:53:47,557
Goodness, just look at your face.

781
00:53:48,850 --> 00:53:51,686
Did you really have to go
all the way to the end?

782
00:53:52,562 --> 00:53:54,522
You could have waited
until you were better.

783
00:53:55,148 --> 00:53:57,525
Did you really
have to go as far as to draw blood?

784
00:53:59,069 --> 00:54:00,153
Because of you, Mom.

785
00:54:01,988 --> 00:54:05,325
If I had a rematch on another day,
you'd have to cry again.

786
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:07,702
Red corner wins by KO!

787
00:54:08,203 --> 00:54:10,247
Advancing to the final, red corner.

788
00:54:17,754 --> 00:54:19,631
Red corner wins by KO!

789
00:54:24,469 --> 00:54:26,720
Seeing you there gave me strength.

790
00:54:26,721 --> 00:54:28,640
That's why I won.

791
00:54:31,017 --> 00:54:32,227
Thanks for coming, Mom.

792
00:54:37,190 --> 00:54:38,191
You rascal.

793
00:54:39,234 --> 00:54:40,734
You rascal!

794
00:54:40,735 --> 00:54:43,280
You damn rascal!

795
00:54:44,239 --> 00:54:47,951
Why did I even give birth to you?

796
00:54:48,535 --> 00:54:49,661
Okay.

797
00:54:50,870 --> 00:54:51,997
It's okay, Mom.

798
00:54:54,708 --> 00:54:56,167
Why did you give birth to me?

799
00:54:56,751 --> 00:54:59,170
So you could see me
win a gold medal, of course.

800
00:55:03,717 --> 00:55:05,634
Good job, my baby.

801
00:55:05,635 --> 00:55:07,262
I'm so proud of you, my son.

802
00:55:08,763 --> 00:55:09,848
I didn't even know

803
00:55:11,266 --> 00:55:13,977
my Pil-seung was this amazing.

804
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:18,732
I'm sorry I didn't know.

805
00:55:22,319 --> 00:55:23,320
It's okay.

806
00:55:40,378 --> 00:55:41,421
You're crying again?

807
00:55:42,839 --> 00:55:45,550
Young man, maybe you should get checked
for menopause?

808
00:55:49,929 --> 00:55:51,848
I'm in my twenties.

809
00:55:54,476 --> 00:55:55,310
What?

810
00:55:57,687 --> 00:55:59,898
- He said he's in his twenties.
- Tae-ha.

811
00:56:04,277 --> 00:56:06,236
- This is perfectly fine.
- Still, stop it.

812
00:56:06,237 --> 00:56:07,696
It'll hurt.

813
00:56:07,697 --> 00:56:10,325
It doesn't hurt. I'm a gold medalist.

814
00:56:16,414 --> 00:56:19,666
- Are we having a feast at Pil-seung's?
- Barbecue?

815
00:56:19,667 --> 00:56:21,001
- Damn right.
- Yeah, let's.

816
00:56:21,002 --> 00:56:22,878
- Hui-ja's treat.
- What are we eating?

817
00:56:22,879 --> 00:56:24,254
Let's just eat at home.

818
00:56:24,255 --> 00:56:26,049
Let's have some barbecue…

819
00:56:26,549 --> 00:56:28,093
They look great.

820
00:56:28,593 --> 00:56:34,224
It feels like I'm watching
a TV show's happy ending.

821
00:56:35,266 --> 00:56:38,395
Wasn't I also like a character
in a TV show today?

822
00:56:39,354 --> 00:56:42,399
Wasn't I sort of awesome earlier?

823
00:56:43,400 --> 00:56:46,653
Where did that come from earlier?
Did you remember something?

824
00:56:49,114 --> 00:56:51,866
I don't really know
where it came from either.

825
00:56:53,034 --> 00:56:57,247
It does sort of feel like
I've done that before.

826
00:56:57,747 --> 00:57:01,584
If I'm honest, I've felt kind of weird
since I got here today.

827
00:57:02,419 --> 00:57:05,004
I feel like I've been here before.

828
00:57:06,256 --> 00:57:09,217
Is this the only boxing arena?

829
00:57:09,968 --> 00:57:11,052
No.

830
00:57:12,220 --> 00:57:14,597
But I like this one the most.

831
00:57:15,557 --> 00:57:16,391
Why?

832
00:57:17,100 --> 00:57:18,351
I met my first love here.

833
00:57:21,396 --> 00:57:24,858
That darn first love of yours
is really getting on my nerves.

834
00:57:29,028 --> 00:57:31,573
<i>It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.</i>

835
00:57:39,080 --> 00:57:40,957
What was his name again?

836
00:57:45,670 --> 00:57:47,297
I want to remember it.

837
00:57:52,510 --> 00:57:54,512
What? Did you remember something else?

838
00:57:55,763 --> 00:57:56,972
Yes.

839
00:57:56,973 --> 00:58:00,435
I think I met some guy here
a long time ago.

840
00:58:03,730 --> 00:58:05,106
Do you remember anything else?

841
00:58:10,653 --> 00:58:11,488
No.

842
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:14,573
I don't remember any details,

843
00:58:14,574 --> 00:58:18,285
but I think that guy was really

844
00:58:18,286 --> 00:58:20,455
handsome.

845
00:58:21,581 --> 00:58:24,918
- What?
- He had a really good vibe, and…

846
00:58:25,502 --> 00:58:26,418
Right!

847
00:58:26,419 --> 00:58:29,130
He said he was a future gold medalist.

848
00:58:29,756 --> 00:58:30,881
Yeah.

849
00:58:30,882 --> 00:58:34,259
And judging by
how I kept glancing back wistfully,

850
00:58:34,260 --> 00:58:37,430
I think I must have liked that guy a lot.

851
00:58:38,056 --> 00:58:39,182
He was handsome.

852
00:58:43,144 --> 00:58:45,896
That's why you should stop
talking about your first love.

853
00:58:45,897 --> 00:58:49,734
I just don't remember him now,
but I had a guy like that too.

854
00:59:00,453 --> 00:59:01,287
Wait for me.

855
00:59:18,846 --> 00:59:21,808
Jang Tae-ha,
I'm off to work at the taffy workshop.

856
01:00:27,457 --> 01:00:28,875
Is this yours, sir?

857
01:00:50,813 --> 01:00:52,482
OUR STICKY LOVE

858
01:01:39,112 --> 01:01:43,074
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
